  "about": {
    "intro": "Advanced view: an ImageJ-style editor for the slice you chose in the Studio. It works on the lossless voxels of the dataset.",
    "source": "Several slices are flattened into one with Z Project; the stored data is 8-bit, so Max and Min stay 8-bit, Sum is 16-bit (exact up to 257 slices), Average, Standard Deviation and Median are 32-bit.",
    "depth": "Display changes (brightness, contrast, lookup tables, threshold overlay) never touch the pixels; Apply, filters and type changes do, and can be undone while memory allows.",
    "deviations": "Differences from ImageJ: Clear and Clear Outside use 0 (black) and Fill uses the maximum value, because fluorescence images have a dark background; Convert to Mask and Threshold Apply create a new image; Sum projection is 16-bit.",
